      "description": "Coker University Resources | Faculty and Staff Info & Links Skip to content Coker University Coker University is a private university in Hartsville, South Carolina. search Search search About expand_more A student-focused, private liberal arts college located in Hartsville, South Carolina. About Coker Overview Why Coker? Strategic Plan 2025-2028 University Leadership Departments & Offices Campus News Campus Map Faculty and Staff Emeriti Academics expand_more Discover the path to your future at Coker University. Academic Overview Coker Academic Programs and Degrees Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs APEC at Coker Honors Program Study Abroad Programs Student Success Writer’s Studio Academic Calendar Admission & Costs expand_more Coker University makes the admissions process seamless for all students. Admission & Aid Overview Freshman Transfer Online and Bridge Programs Graduate Admissions Cost Scholarships Military & Veteran Information Financial Aid Toolkit Net Price Calculator Student Life expand_more With Coker, you’ll find new ideas and a supportive community. Student Life Overview Residence Life and Housing Clubs & Organizations Food Library-Information Technology Center Campus Safety Student Success Campus Center for Health and Wellness Student Accessibility Services Alumni expand_more Welcome home! Thank you for allowing us to be a part of your story! Homecoming Alumni Day Update your Info Awards & Honors Alumni News Alumni Association Board Commentary Magazine Coker Cobra Alumni Business Directory Coker Alumni Attorney Directory Athletics Apply Visit Give Latest Coker News: Coker University Receives NSF Grant to Enhance Research Capacity and Build Sustainable STEM Workforce Pathways in South Carolina Latest: Coker University Receives NSF Grant to Enhance Research Capacity and Build Sustainable STEM Workforce Pathways in South Carolina Apply arrow_forward Visit arrow_forward Give arrow_forward I am: Select  Students Family & Visitors Alumni Faculty & Staff Faculty & Staff FACULTY & STAFF Home / Resources / Faculty & Staff Related Links Ways to Give President’s Home Fundraiser Strategic Plan Coker University Store Faculty and Staff Emeriti Coker University’s 17th President Coker Society What’s new? There’s always something to do at Coker! The campus calendar lists the many upcoming activities, performances, athletic events, presentations, and important occasions. Is something missing? Submit your event !* *Please note that the Office of Marketing & Communications must manually approve campus calendar events , so there may be a brief delay between the time of submission and publication of your event. View Full Calendar of Events Find People add remove Faculty & Staff Directory Search for Coker faculty and staff members by name or department. If you’re a current member of our faculty & staff and wish to update your directory info, please visit the Office of Marketing and Communications page to submit a request. Go To The Directory add remove Campus Map Sometimes, we all need a little geographical assistance! Our interactive campus map will point you in the right direction! Go To Campus Map add remove Faculty and Staff Emeriti View Faculty and Staff Emeriti of Coker University Campus Communication add remove Coker Email Email is an official means of communication at Coker, and since we are a G Suite for Education school, you can access your campus email account directly through Gmail! Go To Coker Email add remove Google Calendar Trying to schedule a meeting with a colleague? Want to reserve a conference room? Our campus is connected with Google Calendar, which offers an easy way to send meeting requests, book available campus spaces, and organize your schedule. Go To Google Calendar add remove COBRAnnouncements Our campus email digest is sent out daily, Monday – Friday, with one edition going to students and another to faculty/staff. See this page for information about when and how to submit your announcement to our campus community. Go To CobrAnnouncements Platforms & Software add remove Brightspace Go To Brightspace add remove CobraStop Go To CobraStop add remove Google Drive Google Drive provides a homebase for all files you create and share through the G Suite for Education, including Google Docs, Google Slides, Google Forms, etc. Go To Google Drive Human Resources, Policies & Employee Organizations add remove iSolved This portal provides access to timesheets, benefits information, W2s, HR-related information and forms for new hires, benefits, campus services, etc. Go To iSolved add remove Title IX As a recipient of Federal Funds, Coker College is required to comply with Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex in educational programs or activities, admission and employment. Visit this page for information about Title IX policies and procedures. Go To Title IX Information add remove FERPA All Coker student records are protected by the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) of 1974. Learn more about FERPA and what it means for your work as a Coker employee. Go To FERPA Information Academic Resources For Faculty & Staff add remove Academic Catalog The academic catalog outlines academic requirements for students in all fields of study across the university. The digital version of this publication serves as an official reference for the institution. Go To Academic Catalogs add remove Academic Calendar Keep track of term/semester start and end dates, add/drop periods, roster verification deadlines, etc. Go To Academic Calendar add remove Library The Coker library is located in the Library-Information Technology Center—but many of their resources are also accessible online! View this page for more information about service hours, research guides, database access, a digital card catalog, or live chat with a librarian. Go To Library Resources Help a Student | Resources For Referral add remove Center for Health & Wellness (Medical & Counseling Services) Located at 212 South 2nd Street, Suite 212 (behind the DeLoach Center), Coker’s Center for Health & Wellness is home to a variety of professional healthcare and mental health counseling services. See their webpage for hours of operation, appointment information, and available services. Go To Center For Health & Wellness add remove Writer’s Studio Need some help with an essay assignment? Want feedback on your research paper outline? The Writer’s Studio tutors can help writers of all skill levels improve the quality of their work. Go To Writer’s Studio add remove Quantitative Literacy Center The Q.L. Center provides math tutoring, in addition to resources like graphic calculators and computers to assist you in your studies. Student and professional staff are available to help you understand and excel at anything related to numbers or mathematics! Go To QL Center Request Campus Services add remove IT Helpdesk View the IT Helpdesk for information about a variety of campus technology topics. You may also use this portal to submit a help ticket or check the status of an existing ticket. You may also email support@coker.edu for assistance. Go To IT Helpdesk add remove Facilities Support Request Form Request maintenance assistance from campus facilities staff by filling out this form. Go To Facilities Support Request Form add remove Bus Request Form If you need to reserve a campus bus for upcoming travel, please fill out this form with the appropriate information. Go To Bus Request Form CONNECT WITH COKER Use #CokerPride to share photos and stories as you prepare to join the Coker community! You can also follow and tag us on Facebook , Twitter , or Instagram . Be part of our community, as we work together to learn, lead, and inspire. Request Information arrow_forward Plan Your Visit arrow_forward Apply 300 E. College Avenue Hartsville, SC 29550 Main: (843) 383-8000 Admissions: (843) 383-8050 Emergency: (843) 383-8140 Visitors Visit Coker Campus Map Cam